  "agent_descriptions": [],
  "final": "I added `ContactStore.find_by_phone(number)` in `contacts/store.py`. It normalizes the query with the same `normalize_phone` that `add` uses, then compares it to the stored numbers. It returns a list of matching contacts, and an empty list if the number isn't a plausible phone number.\n\nI ran it by hand against a contact stored as `(415) 555-0100`. It matched `415-555-0100`, `+1 415 555 0100`, `4155550100` and `1 (415) 555-0100`, and `12` returned `[]`. I didn't add a test to `tests/test_store.py` or run the existing test suite.\n\nI didn't use `clean_phone` in `compat.py`. It only strips non-digits, so `+1 415…` and `415…` wouldn't match each other.",
